  "report": {
    "incident_id": "slack-redirect-046",
    "outcome": "probable_cause",
    "hypotheses": [
      {
        "description": "Most likely cause for the observed failed Slack connection is an OAuth redirect URI mismatch. In the failing production request, the authorization request used /api/v1/auth-apps/add while the registered redirect URI was /api/v3/s/demo, and a controlled comparison shows the same request succeeds when those values match. Scope should remain bounded to the observed failed cedar new-connection flow; the evidence does not prove who changed the setting or that every Slack connection attempt in the window failed.",
        "supporting_evidence": [
          "ev_a7bfa4c88785",
          "ev_d36163f78ef9",
          "ev_5359147b21d4",
          "ev_db879cd0982c",
          "ev_8d28d999665c"
        ],
        "contradicting_evidence": [],
        "confidence": "high",
        "assumptions": [
          "The controlled sandbox comparison verifies the mechanism but is not canonical proof of when or by whom the app configuration changed.",
          "Tenant-level metrics indicate impact in cedar but are not scoped only to Slack connection-creation attempts."
        ]
      },
      {
        "description": "A broad Slack/provider outage is unlikely. The observed error is a specific redirect_uri_mismatch validation failure, another tenant had successful same-window Slack activity, and the controlled comparison flips outcome by changing only redirect configuration.",
        "supporting_evidence": [
          "ev_a7bfa4c88785"
        ],
        "contradicting_evidence": [
          "ev_d36163f78ef9",
          "ev_5359147b21d4",
          "ev_db879cd0982c",
          "ev_8d28d999665c"
        ],
        "confidence": "low",
        "assumptions": [
          "A provider-returned OAuth validation error does not by itself imply provider instability."
        ]
      },
      {
        "description": "An internal change remains unconfirmed as an origin story for why the wrong redirect URI was used, but it is not needed to explain the observed rejection. Supplied telemetry does not show a relevant tool-executor or auth-service deployment, and there is no canonical callback-construction or config-history record here tying the mismatch to an internal regression.",
        "supporting_evidence": [
          "ev_a7bfa4c88785",
          "ev_8d28d999665c"
        ],
        "contradicting_evidence": [
          "ev_d36163f78ef9",
          "ev_4fdcd7693563",
          "ev_19825437f59d",
          "ev_c0e0d72f8607",
          "ev_5359147b21d4"
        ],
        "confidence": "low",
        "assumptions": [
          "Empty deployment query results are not proof that no internal change existed outside supplied telemetry.",
          "The immediate failure mechanism can be diagnosed without proving the source of the misconfiguration."
        ]
      }
    ],
    "recommended_actions": [
      "Proposed only; not executed. Verify the custom Slack OAuth app's registered redirect URI exactly matches the callback URI actually sent by the auth flow, and do not use the short per-connection link as the OAuth redirect URI.",
      "Proposed only; not executed. Identify which tenants/workspaces use the same custom Slack OAuth app and check whether failed new-connection attempts show the same registered-versus-authorization redirect mismatch.",
      "Proposed only; not executed. Separate connection-creation failures from steady-state Slack operations when assessing impact, since same-window evidence shows at least one tenant with healthy existing Slack usage.",
      "Proposed only; not executed. If origin still matters, collect canonical auth-service/setup-flow records or app-settings audit history showing where cedar's authorization_redirect_uri was sourced."
    ],
    "limitations": [
      "Synthetic telemetry was used, including controlled reproduce records; these support the mechanism but are not canonical production proof of configuration history.",
      "The evidence directly verifies the observed cedar failure and a healthy comparison tenant, but does not enumerate all Slack new-connection attempts in the incident window.",
      "Tenant impact metrics are for tool-executor at tenant scope and do not isolate only Slack auth-initiation traffic."
    ]
  },
